# Adversarial log: www test audit pilot, Phase 3, round 5 (confirmation)

Audited head: 496ce2233. Probe commit: 3bad02148.

ADV-15 is closed. The helper fails closed: it throws, naming tag and
property, on an inline --color-* token on the element or an ancestor,
and on a compiled-stylesheet token rule the element matches. The
orchestrator-directed change of the ADV-15 assertion to expect a throw
is sound: a throw is a valid way not to pass silently. The shipped
pricing, contact, and hero surfaces pass with no false throw (25
tests).

One silent pass remains (ADV-17). A colour-token rule injected through
a <style> element at test time is not in the compiled-stylesheet scan,
so a tested element matching it computes from :root without throwing.
The committed probe fails its ADV-17 case until Green scans the
document stylesheets present at read time.

Other helper edge cases are notes: ancestor-matched compiled rules are
not checked (ADV-18), and token rules nested in at-rules are not
scanned (ADV-19).

